  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "20",
  "quote": "Subsection (1) applies even if the tenant was aware of a state of non-repair or a contravention of a standard before entering into the tenancy agreement.",
  "reason": "Under section 20 of the Act, the landlord is responsible for maintaining the rental unit in a good state of repair even if the tenant knew about the defects before signing the lease. By section 4, any provision in a tenancy agreement that conflicts with this statutory obligation is void."
}

